# Telegram credentials for local `tgkb auth` runs (Story 1.3 manual testing).
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your real values:
#     Copy-Item .env.example .env
# Then just run auth -- the CLI auto-loads .env on start (via python-dotenv,
# a dev-only dependency):
#     uv run tgkb auth
#
# Precedence: a variable already set in your shell wins over the .env value,
# so you can still override a single field ad-hoc with `$env:TG_PHONE=...`.
#
# `.env` is gitignored -- it holds a secret (TG_API_HASH) and must never be
# committed. This `.env.example` is the tracked, secret-free template.
#
# Get api_id / api_hash from https://my.telegram.org -> "API development tools".
# These env vars are now the FIRST-RUN bootstrap only: on first `tgkb auth` they
# supply the credentials, which are then persisted encrypted at rest
# (.tgkb-data/session.enc, Story 1.4). On later runs the tool reuses that
# passphrase-protected session and reads api_id/api_hash/phone from it — no env
# vars needed. Keep .env for a convenient first run or a fresh re-auth.

TG_API_ID=1234567
TG_API_HASH=your_api_hash_here
TG_PHONE=+79991234567
